    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Soderstrom** leads the charge with an elite 76.91 score, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Meibrys Kelly (5.31 xERA) and the significant bump provided by his spot in the two-hole. He is joined at the top of our priority list by **James Wood** (71.14) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.64). Both benefit from high park-factor adjustments (+14%) and premium lineup positioning. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a set-and-forget anchor, leveraging a massive +14% platoon edge against a right-handed arm to reach a strong 70.68 score. While **Corbin Carroll** sits just below the 60 threshold, his elite sprint speed remains our highest priority in this 5x5 Roto format; despite a tougher matchup against Jump, his potential to manufacture runs on the basepaths necessitates his inclusion over lower-ceiling alternatives.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Naylor**, who posted a respectable 63.11 score. While he grades out better than several active starters, he was ultimately sidelined due to a confluence of a pitcher-friendly park and a poor BvP track record across 44 plate appearances against Brady Singer. Conversely, **Jose Caballero** remains active despite a defensive platoon penalty (-13%) because the significant SP skill advantage provided by Mitch Keller (+18%) keeps his floor elevated above our available reserves. We are closely monitoring the weather for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll**, as their matchup against Jump involves a slightly restrictive environment, though we expect no lineup disruptions. Our aggressive focus on park-adjusted upside and leadoff efficiency gives Ghost Ride the WHIP a distinct advantage today, provided our speed-first assets like **James Wood** can capitalize on their high-percentage opportunities.",
